      "explanation": "The scenario is suggestive of meralgia paresthetica, in which the lateral cutaneous nerve of the thigh is affected. Its root value is L2 and L3.\n\nIt arises from the posterior divisions of the ventral rami of L2 and L3 and supplies the skin of the anterior and lateral surfaces of the thigh up to the knee."
